The Killer Mirror

A man lived in a village with his wife. Although they had little money, they were a happy family.

One day, the man bought a mirror for his wife. He gave it to her before leaving for work.

About five hours later, some of her friends invited her to a small restaurant. She quickly got ready, took the new mirror, and looked at herself.

Then she saw something horrifying.

Standing behind her in the mirror was a very tall, extremely thin humanoid.

The woman quickly put the mirror down and checked the room around her. There was nothing there. She looked into the mirror again, but the humanoid was gone.

She thought it had only been her imagination.

After getting dressed and putting on makeup, she left the house and met her friends. They went to a small restaurant and sat down.

Suddenly, she saw the same humanoid again.

It rushed toward her at incredible speed and broke her neck.

Her friends were terrified. Her body was facing forward, while her head had been twisted backward.

The humanoid could only be seen by the person who looked into the mirror.

Later, the woman's husband returned from work. He looked into the mirror and saw something completely different.

There was a strange baby lying on the bed behind him.

He immediately turned around and looked at the bed.

There was no baby.

Terrified, he took the mirror down to the basement and buried it.

But when he turned around, the baby was standing behind him.

The baby bit him directly on the neck.

His skin began to shrivel as if all the water had been drained from his body. His bones became visible, and eventually, he died.

The truth was that the mirror could create a dangerous, physical version of a person's deepest fear.

The woman's deepest fear was a tall man who struggled with alcoholism and repeatedly appeared in her life.

The man's deepest fear was his first child, who had died during birth.

The mirror transformed those fears into deadly entities.

Before his death, the man wrote a warning on a piece of paper:

“DO NOT OPEN THIS AT ALL.”

And that was the end of the story.
